{"ornamental":{"id":"8eac4bee-de79-47b5-8be1-13d8ee67d043","word":"ornamental","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"serving to ornament","word":"ornamental"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Some think it most ornamental to wear their bracelets on their wrists; others, about their ankles.","bold_text_offsets":[[19,29]],"type":"example","id":"b6afefc7-d2a5-4654-945b-be4f87fac5c9"},{"text":"We shall leave to the reader to determine with what judgment we have chosen the several occasions for inserting those ornamental parts of our work.","ref":"1749, Henry Fielding, chapter I, in The History of Tom Jones, a Foundling, volume (please specify |volume=I to VI), London: A[ndrew] Millar, […], →OCLC, book IV:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[118,128]],"id":"b433b241-bfaf-45c0-ab6b-1957bce71b2f"},{"text":"There were ornamental ponds and shrubs clipped into animal shapes, painted concrete gnomes sitting on mushrooms, pink flamingos standing on one leg[.]","ref":"1968, Carl Ruhen, The Key Club, Sydney: Scripts, page 20:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[11,21]],"id":"b9314e01-fe74-4edb-9236-aded4138fcc2"}],"links":[["ornament","ornament"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"beautifying"},{"word":"embellishing"},{"word":"decorative"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"glosses":["Serving as an ornament; having no purpose other than to make more beautiful."],"id":"9bd5fcde-31fa-4caf-aacb-5d57709d3b18"},{"examples":[{"text":"Those pine trees on the lawn are the fastest-growing ornamentals we could find.","bold_text_offsets":[[53,64]],"type":"example","id":"b048fd68-25fa-449f-be2d-35e9a441ffa1"}],"topics":["biology","fish","ichthyology","natural-sciences","zoology"],"links":[["Bred","breed"],["aesthetic","aesthetic"],["decorative","decorative"],["purpose","purpose"]],"raw_glosses":["(of a plant, fish, etc.) Bred for aesthetic or decorative purposes."],"glosses":["Bred for aesthetic or decorative purposes."],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"tags":["usually"],"raw_tags":["of a plant"],"id":"d302a500-4848-4caa-9cb7-2e0cb75afbe6"}],"related":[{"word":"ornamentation"},{"word":"ornamentally"}],"synonyms":[]},"ornament":{"id":"61da9e4e-d234-4d21-901e-5431a37dfb45","word":"ornament","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"to decorate","word":"ornamentar"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"to decorate","word":"ornar"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"to decorate","word":"decorar"}],"pos":"verb","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"We will ornament the windows with trim to make the room seem brighter.","bold_text_offsets":[[8,16]],"type":"example","id":"e6073bf5-7ba8-4616-9b9e-46cd0315ee55"},{"text":"After this, perhaps, the next most imposing structure in Liverpool is the railway station; it is built of stone, richly ornamented with thirty-six columns of the Corinthian order.","ref":"1958 October 15, “Liverpool to London in 1842”, in Railway Magazine, page 679:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[120,130]],"id":"7107783f-5ab2-4339-99d0-dad913454b0a"}],"senseid":["en:to decorate"],"links":[["decorate","decorate"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"glosses":["To decorate."],"id":"d0b5a07d-2acf-4fe4-bfcb-a8e78df46d20"},{"examples":[{"text":"The editor ornamented his plain writing, making it fancier but less clear.","bold_text_offsets":[[11,21]],"type":"example","id":"9117438d-d502-4ac0-9e84-d258b2ee5ead"},{"text":"Not a scene goes by that hasn't been ornamented with a split screen, a freeze frame, a caption, a voice-over, a switch between monochrome and colour, or a change of the aspect radio^([sic – meaning ratio]).","ref":"2021 July 12, Nicholas Barber, “The French Dispatch: Four stars for Wes Anderson's latest”, in BBC:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[37,47]],"id":"24246a5f-4802-4d2e-a05b-4073f432c2ed"}],"senseid":["en:to add to"],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"glosses":["To add to."],"id":"48babc42-4f0b-4aed-ae4a-7a16b43c5546"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[{"sense":"decorate","word":"adorn"},{"sense":"decorate","word":"bedeck"},{"sense":"decorate","word":"decorate"},{"sense":"decorate","word":"embellish"},{"sense":"decorate","word":"trim"}]},"ornithopter":{"id":"3d8ae597-4d42-4582-a35e-d933b75684d0","word":"ornithopter","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"aircraft that flaps its wings","tags":["masculine"],"word":"ornitóptero"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"links":[["aircraft","aircraft"],["lift","lift"],["flap","flap"]],"glosses":["An aircraft that generates lift through the flapping of its wings."],"categories":["English countable nouns","English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English nouns","English terms derived from Ancient Greek","English terms derived from French","English terms prefixed with ornitho-","English terms suffixed with -pter","English undefined derivations","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Terms with Afrikaans translations","Terms with Armenian translations","Terms with Catalan translations","Terms with Esperanto translations","Terms with Finnish translations","Terms with French translations","Terms with German translations","Terms with Greek translations","Terms with Italian translations","Terms with Norwegian translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Romanian translations","Terms with Russian translations","Terms with Serbo-Croatian translations","Terms with Spanish translations","Terms with Turkish translations","en:Aviation"],"id":"3f2adddc-4d7f-4523-9715-aadf09f1b243"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"ornamentation":{"id":"0c65d307-fcc4-4f7c-a2ef-9bb352687cd6","word":"ornamentation","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt"